{"availability":"available","full":"starkience/shadow-account-demo","name":"shadow-account-demo","description":"Developer example: use a Starknet shadow account to hold a Vesu Prime vSTRK vault position.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-29T07:56:47Z","updated":"2026-10-07T11:54:32Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://shadow-account-demo.vercel.app","topics":["defi","privacy","react","shadow-accounts","starknet","strk20","vesu"],"demo":"https://shadow-account-demo.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:47:43.413Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:47:43.413Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:47:43.413Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:21.562Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T23:47:43.413Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A developer example showing how a Starknet shadow account can own a persistent position in the existing Vesu Prime vSTRK vault.","The dapp connects to a privacy-enabled wallet through Starknet.js WalletAccountV6. The wallet handles private state, proof generation, fees, and submission. The application builds ordinary Starknet calls and hands them to the wallet as native STRK20ACTION[].","This repository uses live Mainnet contracts and real assets. It is an educational integration example, not audited production software."],"features":["The wallet owns the privacy machinery. The dapp never handles viewing","The canonical ShadowAccountAnonymizer is shared infrastructure. The","The shadow account makes ordinary Starknet calls. Vesu already exposes","The integration is two explicit action arrays. The important code lives"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/starkience/shadow-account-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"66736ab779eebbad6118be6681b760459fc1465e5ad10923fa20b3ebe1a711d8","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:21.962Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:2